## Pretty Code

\`\`\`javascript {1|4-8}{lines:true}
import React, { useState } from 'react';

function Example() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

  return (
    <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>Clicked {count} times</button>
  );
}
\`\`\`

Code syntax highlighting courtesy of [highlight.js](https://highlightjs.org/usage/).

---

## Markdown support

Write content using inline or external Markdown.

- **Bold** and _italic_ text
- <Click as="span">A [link](https://revealjs.com)</Click>
- Inline \`code\`

<Notes>

These notes are written in Markdown.

</Notes>

---

## External Markdown

Slides can live in a Markdown file of their own.

- Loaded with \`data-markdown="assets/notes.md"\`
- Split on a line of three dashes

<Notes>

These notes come from the external file.

</Notes>

---

## A second external slide

\`\`\`js {1|3-4}{lines:true}
const deck = await load("notes.md");

deck.slides.forEach((slide) => {
  render(slide);
});
\`\`\`

